2186294233 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "556a7d43-607a-51f8-bbc7-32726ebb62ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294486 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186292972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294486 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294486 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294486 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186292972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294486 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9af6deca-2a10-5fc3-bd8b-495794517f17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294800 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186293816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294800 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294800 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294800 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186293816 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186294800 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f7dbeb64-58f8-574e-b5ca-1af2fbe26d0e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295118 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295118 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294233 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295118 #edb/ref 1069 "q-280223" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295118 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295118 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation ${y}^{2}=-8x.$ Express your answer in the form $x=p{t}^{2},y=2pt,$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295118 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "09e9d4e7-4fc4-5d2a-8e90-c6b221db0edc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295118 #edb/ref 1074 "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola ${y}^{2}=4px$ that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case ${y}^{2}=4px$ and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4px & =-8x \\\\ 4p & =-8 \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(-2){t}^{2},\\,y=2(-2)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=-2{t}^{2},\\,y=-4t.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295119 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186293948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295119 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295119 #edb/ref 1069 "q-280226" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295119 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295119 #edb/ref 1071 "Determine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation ${y}^{2}=32x.$ Express your answer in the form $x=p{t}^{2},y=2pt,$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295119 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "661e8b2f-b39b-52c7-a534-20b19b10d577" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295119 #edb/ref 1074 "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola ${y}^{2}=4px$ that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case ${y}^{2}=4px$ and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4px & =32x \\\\ 4p & =32 \\\\ p & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(8){t}^{2},\\,y=2(8)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=8{t}^{2},\\,y=16t.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295121 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295121 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186294800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295121 #edb/ref 1069 "q-280233" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295121 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295121 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d8/d8e4aa88acf2a0d69d4c4208dc4951a33cc92e59e177395ec74be3ae0f9a8c7f.png)\n\nDetermine a set of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ that generate the parabola shown above. Express your answer in the form $x=p{t}^{2},y=2pt,$ where $p$ is a constant.\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}},\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295121 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "101558b0-e03b-5b3f-a1c3-2d14536fe534" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186295121 #edb/ref 1074 "The diagram shows that the parabola is horizontal, has its vertex at $(0,0),$ and passes through the point $(-5,-4).$\n\nThe parametric equations of a horizontal parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nSince the parabola passes through $(-5,-4),$ we can substitute $x=-5$ and $y=-4$ into the standard parametric equations to obtain a system of equations. This gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5 &=p{t}^{2} \\\\ -4 &=2pt.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSolving the second equation for $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4 & =2pt \\\\ t & =-\\frac{2}{p}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the first equation and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5 & =p{(-\\frac{2}{p})}^{2} \\\\ -5 & =p\\cdot \\frac{4}{{p}^{2}} \\\\ p & =-\\frac{4}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(-\\frac{4}{5}){t}^{2},\\,y=2(-\\frac{4}{5})t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{4}{5}{t}^{2},\\,y=-\\frac{8}{5}t.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186351890 #edb/ref 1080 "{y}^{2}=12x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351890 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351890 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "239ab912-cfd2-52df-b992-7ed2e7c2727b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352233 #edb/ref 1080 "{y}^{2}=6x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352233 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352233 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "48369b80-33d6-5dff-b595-9ed79809a5e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352235 #edb/ref 1080 "{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186352235 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 1